      "writtenOn": "2020-10-29T23:09:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t it both less fragile and easier to consume the XML output, i.e. \"dexdump -l xml foo.jar\", and then use an XML parser? E.g. with xml.etree.ElementTree is a simple one (http://go/pylib/xml.etree.elementtree.html#module-xml.etree.ElementTree) you should get the package names you want pretty easily with something like this (untested):\n\n  root \u003d xml.etree.ElementTree.fromstring(stdout)\n  for package_elt in root.iterfind(\u0027package\u0027):\n    package_name \u003d package_elt.get(\u0027name\u0027)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "ed722313d53b3257ae7314d75aebfab3a8fc592d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
