      "writtenOn": "2020-10-30T16:09:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e XML output is far more verbose\n\nThat could be a factor, but if it outweighs the benefits can be discussed. In the random example I tried (libcore/core-oj/android_common/dex/classes.dex.jar) the XML is actually smaller, I think because it doesn\u0027t contain the same amount of detail. But that may very well not be representative at all.\n\n\u003e I tried as you suggested but it failed because of http://b/172042691.\n\nAha, I\u0027d work around that by constructing a root element:\n\n```\n\u003e\u003e\u003e fragment \u003d \u0027\u003cfoo\u003e\u003cbar x\u003d\"a\"/\u003e\u003c/foo\u003e\u003cfoo\u003e\u003cbar x\u003d\"b\"/\u003e\u003c/foo\u003e\u0027\n\u003e\u003e\u003e root \u003d xml.etree.ElementTree.fromstring(\u0027\u003croot\u003e\u0027 + fragment + \u0027\u003c/root\u003e\u0027)\n\u003e\u003e\u003e [e.get(\u0027x\u0027) for e in root.iterfind(\u0027foo/bar\u0027)]\n[\u0027a\u0027, \u0027b\u0027]\n```\n\nShouldn\u0027t require any change later if the XML output is fixed, provided it stays compatible.",
      "parentUuid": "2e95c5c3_bde82b0f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 28,
